<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 3 Best in Slot Gear list for Balance Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Trial of the Grand Crusader. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Balance Druid DPS Phase 3</h2>In phase 3, Balance will reach all soft caps, though this does not necessarily change how we gear. You should always aim to meet the required Hit rating. If you are fully talented into <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33596/balance-of-power">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_balanceofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Balance of Power</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33602/improved-faerie-fire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Improved Faerie Fire</span></a>, you only need 10% Hit from gear (263 rating) to reach the hit cap requirement for a boss fight. Furthermore, if you play for the Alliance, Draenei provide <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=28878/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> to their party members, bringing your required Hit to 9% (236 rating).<br/>
<br/>As always, crit continues to be a very strong stat for Balance. In Phase 3 we will reach a mana neutral to mana positive state, and with the lack of trash in ToGC, it is highly unlikely that we will need to use <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=29166/innervate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_lightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Innervate</span></a> on ourselves.<br/>
<br/>2 piece Tier 9 provides a nice boost to dps by allowing our <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48463/moonfire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_starfall.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Moonfire</span></a> DoT to crit. This also leads to rotational and glyph changes that you can find in the rotation guide.<br/>
<br/>If you find your raid is unable to kill the heroic versions of the bosses, the normal variants drop items of the same name but lower item level and those items can be substituted though you may have to gem toward more hit rating.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended Gear progression is: T8 -&gt; 2pcT9+2pcT8 -&gt; 4pcT9</b>
<br/>
<br/>There are two sets listed below, one assumes horde while the other assumes Alliance WITH <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a>. On the Horde BiS List, you will notice a few orange gems, in this case <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40152/potent-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Potent Ametrine</span></a>. These gems are interchangeable with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40113/runed-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runed Cardinal Ruby</span></a> in these slots and provide near-equal dps.<br/>
<br/>These sets assume you have access to Engineering and Tailoring, the former being highly recommended. For more information on other options for individual slots, read the sections below.<br/>
<br/>
